# fdth — acronyms mirror (regra de ouro)

Project glossary lives as a **full language mirror** under `acronyms/`:

| Pack | File | Language |
|------|------|----------|
| PT-BR | `acronyms/acronyms_pt.txt` | Portuguese Brazil (owner preference) |
| EN | `acronyms/acronyms_en.txt` | English |
| Compat stub | `acronyms/acronyms.txt` | Pointer only — not the body |

## Norm (permanent)

1. **Same keys / ids / paths** in both twins (CP, VCP, VP-FDTH, …). Translate
   **prose only**; keep acronym tokens identical.
2. **Any add / edit / rename / delete** of an entry must update **both**
   twins in the **same task** — no single-language drift.
3. Twin headers must cross-point (`Twin (PT-BR): …` / `Gémeo (EN): …`) and
   share the same `Updated:` / `Atualizado:` date when content changes.
4. Do **not** put glossary body back into `acronyms/acronyms.txt` (stub only).
5. When citing the glossary to the owner, prefer **PT**
   (`acronyms/acronyms_pt.txt`). EN for international / GitHub readers.
6. New languages only on explicit request (same mirror discipline as
   `w_todo`).
7. Root folder is **`acronyms/`**. Packs: `acronyms_en.txt` and
   `acronyms_pt.txt`.

## Reading preference

- Owner: PT (`acronyms/acronyms_pt.txt`).
- EN remains first-class (`acronyms/acronyms_en.txt`).
